Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all,
my app uses numerous tabs and dynamic-generated input. Here is a reproductible example :

library(shiny)
ui = function(request) {
  fluidPage(
    navbarPage(
      title = "test",
      id = "main",
      tabPanel("tab1",
               uiOutput("renderTab1")),
      tabPanel("tab2",
               uiOutput("renderTab2")),
      footer = bookmarkButton()
    )
  )
}
server <- shinyServer(function(session, input, output) {
  output$renderTab1 <- renderUI({
    tagList(
      textInput("text1", "Write your text", ""),
      actionButton("ok", "OK")
    )
  })

  output$renderTab2 <- renderUI({
    h3(input$text1)
  })

  observeEvent(input$ok, {
    updateTabsetPanel(session, "main", "tab2")
  })
})
enableBookmarking(store = "url")
shinyApp(ui, server)

When I restore a session from a bookmarked state, inputs are not updated as long as I have not selected the tab where the input is located (in that example, I need to select tab1 in order to display h3(input$text1)).

As a workaround, I'm using delay(1, updateTabsetPanel("tab")), but maybe there is a better solution for that problem?

Best regards

